From 6e3a2418338f16a4b9650f289e76c3cc7d240008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 17:56:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] first boot: one Reaper box sets the Wi-Fi name, the Wi-Fi
 password and the router login

The security banner's Wi-Fi step pointed at the stock Wireless page, which shows
the PRIMARY BSS settings; on this build the primaries become the hidden AiMesh
backhaul and the user's network lives on the wlN.1 fronthaul VIFs, rebuilt by
cfg_server after a plain wireless apply. Filling that page in and hoping the
migration follows was the clunky part of a factory box.

Reaper_WiFiSetup.asp replaces it as the banner target: network name, Wi-Fi
password and router login password in one step. reaper_wifisetup.cgi (gated on
http_id, do_auth) writes for every radio exactly what the stock apply writes -
one SSID and key, psk2sae on 2.4/5 GHz, sae on 6 GHz, protected management
frames, the crypto suite the radio's WiFi 7 mode selects, hidden off, Smart
Connect on with the interface mask computed by the js/asus.js rule - then
commits and returns. It never restarts anything itself. The page changes the
login through httpApi.chpass first (it needs the current session), then the
CGI, then one start_apply with "saveNvram;restart_chpass;restart_wireless", so
the radios restart only after the password is committed and shadow rebuilt
(reaper-ui rule 28). A refused password stops everything; a refused Wi-Fi
setting still persists the password change.

The key bound (8..63 printable or 64 hex) is enforced in the page AND the CGI:
hostapd accepts nothing else and then runs with no key line, which killed every
band in v2.9.1. The stock Wireless page is untouched and stays for engineers.

13 RWFS_ tokens, English-seeded in all 25 packs (lockstep 6860). Page in
reaper_skip[] + reaper_css_only[] like Main_Password.asp.
