+RWFS_3=Wi-Fi password
+RWFS_4=8 to 63 characters. This is what people type to join the network.
+RWFS_5=Router login password
+RWFS_6=This is what you type to open these pages. Keep it different from the Wi-Fi password.
+RWFS_7=Show passwords
+RWFS_8=Set up and restart Wi-Fi
+RWFS_9=The Wi-Fi password must be 8 to 63 characters (or a 64-digit hexadecimal key).
+RWFS_10=The network name must be 1 to 32 characters.
+RWFS_11=Done. Wi-Fi is restarting as %1$@ - reconnect to it, then log in with your new router password.
+RWFS_12=The router refused the Wi-Fi settings:
+RWFS_13=Using the same password for Wi-Fi and for the router login is not recommended. Continue anyway?
